course: dictionary
lesson: 15739
title: Transparency: see-through and open
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Transparency comes from the word transparent, which means you can see clearly through something, like clean glass or still water.
explain: The word also means being open and honest, so people can see what is happening and why. «The club shared every bill with its members, which showed real transparency.» Here the clues are shared and bill: nobody is hiding anything.
explain: A transparency can also be an old-fashioned clear plastic sheet, shown with an overhead projector. The words around it tell you which meaning is right, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Transparency means being see-through, letting light pass so you can see clearly through something.
fact: «The clear water in the pond had great transparency, so we could see the fish.»
fact: Transparency also means being open and honest, so people can see what is happening and why.
fact: «The leader showed transparency by explaining every decision to the town.»
fact: A transparency can also be a clear plastic sheet with words or pictures on it, used with an overhead projector.
exercise: «The glass in the window has great transparency.» What does transparency mean here? | *Being see-through, so light passes and you can see clearly | Being the colour of the sky | Being hard to break | Being very loud and noisy
exercise: «The council shared every spending figure, which showed real transparency.» What does transparency mean here? | Being made of glass | *Being open and honest so people can see what is happening | Being very quiet
exercise: Tom says a transparency is always made of glass. Which sentence is true? | A transparency is a type of wild animal | *A transparency can be a clear plastic sheet shown on a projector | A transparency must be made of wood | A transparency is always a bright colour
test: Which of these has the most transparency? | Wood | Metal | *Clean glass | Brick
test: «The head teacher explained the rules so that parents could trust the school.» Which idea does this show? | Colour | Speed | Loudness | *Openness and honesty
exam: In science, a material that lets you see clearly through it is said to have high what? | Colour | Weight | *Transparency | Opacity
